  "privacyLocalTitle": "Local mode (without an account)",
  "@privacyLocalTitle": {
    "description": "Privacy policy section title (G40)"
  },
  "privacyLocalBody": "If you use MoneyLedger without a Matrix account, groups you don't share send nothing: for them the app contacts no server and nothing is synced (the web version is only loaded from the site that hosts it). A group you share with an invite link syncs through public Nostr relays (see “Shared groups (invite link)”). Links you tap, e.g. to the source code, open in your browser. Your name, groups, expenses and payments are stored only in a local database on this device, plus a small preferences file (whether you saw the welcome, your local profile name). Deleting local data in the settings, or uninstalling the app, removes them. If you later connect a Matrix account, the local data moves into that account and from then on the sections above apply.",
  "@privacyLocalBody": {
    "description": "Privacy policy section body (G40)"
  },
