  "privacyRestorePointsTitle": "Restore points on this device",
  "@privacyRestorePointsTitle": {
    "description": "Privacy policy section title (G48)"
  },
  "privacyRestorePointsBody": "To let you undo mistakes, MoneyLedger keeps earlier versions of your groups' entries on this device for 90 days, and on Android once a day (when something changed) a copy of all your groups in the app's private storage — the last 7 days plus 4 older weeks. These versions and copies are never sent anywhere, are not part of any backup file, and are excluded from Android's backups like all app data. Leaving or deleting a group removes its earlier versions at once; the daily copies still contain it until they rotate out (after about five weeks), so that a group deleted by mistake can be restored. Deleting local data, or uninstalling the app, removes all of them.",
