  "privacyReceiptsTitle": "Receipt photos (Android)",
  "@privacyReceiptsTitle": {
    "description": "G78 privacy policy section title"
  },
  "privacyReceiptsBody": "On Android you can attach a photo of the receipt to an expense, taken with your camera app or picked from your photos. MoneyLedger stores a smaller copy only in the app's private storage on this device. It is never sent anywhere — not to the others in the group, not to any homeserver — is not part of any backup file, restore point or CSV, and is excluded from Android's backups like all app data. It is deleted with its expense (the next time the app starts), when you leave or delete the group, and when you delete local data or uninstall the app; signing out keeps it. The camera and photo picker are Android's own: MoneyLedger asks for no camera or storage permission and only receives the one photo you choose.",
