  },
  "createGroupShareByLinkBody": "Others join without an account. Anyone with the link can see and change the group. Off: you invite Matrix accounts (secure).",
  "@createGroupShareByLinkBody": {
    "description": "G52 step 6: subtitle of the create-group switch"
  },
  "linkMembersHint": "Shared with a link: people are added by name. Whoever opens the invite link picks who they are.",
  "@linkMembersHint": {
    "description": "G52: hint card on the people page of a link group"
  },
  "privacyLinkTitle": "Shared groups (invite link)",
  "@privacyLinkTitle": {
    "description": "G52: privacy policy section title (keep in sync with PRIVACY.md)"
  },
  "privacyLinkBody": "A group you share with an invite link syncs through public Nostr relays — by default nos.lol and nostr.mom, which have one operator. They are independent services with their own terms. You can change the relays under Settings → Relays: adding one first asks it for its information page (NIP-11), then your shared groups sync through it too. Every device in the group publishes its copy of the group there, encrypted (AES-256-GCM) with a key that only the link contains; the key never goes to a relay or to any server of ours. The relays can't read names, amounts or notes, but they see your device's IP address, when it syncs, roughly how large the group is and how many devices take part, and that the data comes from MoneyLedger. We ask them to delete each copy after 30 days (renewed while the group is in use), but relays may keep or archive data longer — and anyone who gets the link, now or later, can read and change the group, also from archived copies. When you delete a shared group from this device (or delete local data), the app first asks the relays to delete your copy; the others in the group keep theirs. Resetting the invite link (or switching to a new link someone sent you) asks the relays to delete your copy under the old link and publishes the group under a new key; people who only have the old link no longer get your changes, but keep what they already saw. A group only on this device never contacts a relay: a group starts syncing only when you invite with a link, create it with “Share with an invite link” or join it with a link someone sent you. Opening an invite link contacts nothing until you tap “Join”; the relays are then asked for that group.",
  "@privacyLinkBody": {
    "description": "G52: privacy policy section body (keep in sync with PRIVACY.md)"
  },
